  "style": {
    "name": "Warm Analogous Pineapple — Ripe Fruit in the Round",
    "rationale": "Two stacked masses make it instantly nameable from any side: a circular ovoid-of-revolution fruit body (yellow_terracotta, widest ~16 dia at ~40% height, tapering to ~10 at the shoulders, built as stacked per-row disc fills so it reads identically front/side/3-4) and a radiating green_concrete leaf crown flaring up-and-out like a flame. Body height split ~5:18:9 over 32 (base y0-1, body y2-19, crown y20-31) on a flattened 2-block disc base wider than the body bottom for a non-tippy footing. Motif A, the diamond lattice 'eyes', is orange_terracotta diamonds set proud on the shell in a staggered radial grid — mid-band on the four cardinals, a lower band rotated onto the four 45-degree corners, and an upper band back on the cardinals — so the offset rows read as the unmistakable cross-hatch from every angle. Motif B, leaf ridging, is 1-block-thick fins: a tall central tuft plus four cardinal blades splaying out on 45-degree lines with stepped tips, and four shorter diagonal blades to the corners, never merged into a solid cap, giving a jagged green star silhouette. Palette honors the warm yellow-orange-green analogous band with lime_terracotta used sparingly only on the tallest leaf tips. The hidden back half mirrors the visible features so it reads as a finished solid object in the round, not a facade."
  },
